 "premises": {
  "P1_register": "two seam objects, C on the seam (2, 3) and E on the seam (2, 10), each with its own load, record and two-orientation address; a neutral register F carrying the third-turn R of the face (4, 5, 11); T applies R or R^-1 when C repairs at orientation + or -; the clock K_theta = exp(i theta J) acts on the oriented current J = |1><1|_(r_C) sigma_z(o_C); V is the oriented record, Z_r at the reversed address",
  "P2_preparation_and_analyzer": "each object starts with activity 1/3, its load at the screen tail of its seam, a blank record and the uniform address; the analyzer is the Fourier zero over the flags E agrees with C idle, C repairs + with E idle, and C repairs - with E idle",
  "P3_double_load_objects": "two independent hexagon objects, each with two loads, the four-valued record of the public completion and its own twelve-address register reflected about its uniform state; the standing state S = (D_2 + D_10)/sqrt2 has blank records",
  "P4_weak_round": "a round is one tick, the kick exp(-i h J (x) Qx) on the exclusive read Qx of fresh records, the inverse tick and a return test projecting on the standing state; N rounds per unit clock time with h = 1/N",
  "P5_declared_clock": "the clock H = sum_x (I - Re U_x) + sum_edges (pi/4) dGamma(I - S_xy) with evolution exp(-i t H), as declared in model/coherent_defect_wave/energy",
  "P6_oriented_toggle": "the named interaction T(eta) = exp(i eta J (x) Z_F Z_I) between the clocked register and the flags of the pair",
  "P7_two_cells": "two cells with independent sixty-address registers, each holding two loads moved by the public completion at the addressed seam in the order of the address",
  "P8_flux": "a class-k flux through the hexagon is the link phase exp(i pi k/3) on the hexagon seam (2, 3), entering as the gauge conjugation of the completion at both addresses of that seam",
  "P9_return_test_and_shared_kick": "the return test of a cell is the projector on its uniform address state, and a cell is prepared in that state again after a \"no\"; with n partners the kick is the generator (1/n) sum_l Qx_l"
 },
